    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "How much do two weeks in Thailand cost?",
        "main_title": "How much do two weeks in Thailand cost?",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Fluorescent face paint. Bunk beds in dormitories. Whisky served up in plastic buckets on moon-lit stretches of sand. It’s been two decades since my first visit to Thailand: the country was part of a year-long backpacking trip when my only financial concerns were when to splash out on a private room with aircon and when to opt for a cheaper shared room with a barely whirring fan.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Things have changed somewhat since that first visit. I’ve since travelled to Thailand for work, on numerous holidays with my partner and most recently with our toddler. As a more - let’s say - “grown up” traveller, my priorities have shifted – things like clean sheets and money security are more important (hats off to Starling for the 24/7 customer support).",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "But you’ll still find me seeking out the £1 pad thais on a street stall – this is a country where you can eat some of your life’s most memorable meals for a couple of quid. That’s just one part of why I head back every January in a desperate bid to escape the worst of the UK winter. Here’s what I recommend budgeting for a two-week trip, provided you book flights in advance. I’ve included a range, depending on what you’re after.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "And here’s a snapshot of real costs from a recent family trip to the capital and two islands…",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
